.SS "int libusb_has_capability (uint32_t capability)"

.PP
Check at runtime if the loaded library has a given capability\&. This call should be performed after \fBlibusb_init_context()\fP, to ensure the backend has updated its capability set\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcapability\fP the \fBlibusb_capability\fP to check for 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
nonzero if the running library has the capability, 0 otherwise 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char * libusb_error_name (int error_code)"

.PP
Returns a constant NULL-terminated string with the ASCII name of a libusb error or transfer status code\&. The caller must not free() the returned string\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIerror_code\fP The \fBlibusb_error\fP or \fBlibusb_transfer_status\fP code to return the name of\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The error name, or the string \fBUNKNOWN\fP if the value of error_code is not a known error / status code\&. 
.RE
.PP

